acceptance_criteria: "Expose bounded executable discovery for the requested declaration kind, preserve the selected tracker, and identify the rejected ID; prove show/promote SDK, CLI and MCP refusals leave registry/history bytes unchanged; retain typed remove behavior and unexpected corruption/I/O/provider faults; negative controls prove expected misses are excluded from unexpected-fault capture; preserve public SDK compatibility."
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Missing assurance show/promote declarations now expose changed=false, the rejected ID and an executable bounded discovery command for the requested kind in the selected tracker, using the existing SDK action transport and typed refusal without changing public SDK signatures."
expected_result: "Agents recover by listing relevant configured declarations in the selected tracker; expected misses never mutate registry/history or become unexpected Sentry faults, while genuine corruption, I/O and runtime faults remain distinct."
actual_result: "All 38 linked sandbox tests pass, including selected-tracker replay and all-file byte preservation; built Node/Bun each pass seven refusal controls and public SDK/action/MCP checks. Four recovery regressions failed before the patch. Build, typecheck, targeted lint and unchanged public SDK contract pass. Source correction is Unreleased pending final current-head CI, review and merge in PR #1526."
